  2. Tiny samples → noise that dips below 0.5. Each fold tests only ~74 rows. Look at the per-fold  swings: TSLA goes 0.30 → 0.67. That's sampling noise sloshing around 0.5; some folds land below
  by chance, pulling the mean under. A sub-0.5 mean here means "no signal," not "anti-signal."
  3. Likely overfitting. 200 trees at depth 4 on ~370 training rows with 25 features will memorize  noise and generalize at ~chance on single names. (It doesn't hurt the indices because there's
